# Trivy ignore list for the container images (REL-001 / SEC-011).
#
# These advisories are in the BASE IMAGE's Python build tooling
# (pip / setuptools / its vendored jaraco.context / wheel), which lives
# in the system site-packages of python:3.11-slim-bookworm. Our services
# run from the self-contained /app/.venv and NEVER invoke pip, setuptools,
# or wheel at runtime — the builder stage that used them is discarded — so
# these "process a malicious tar/wheel archive" flaws are not reachable in
# the running container.
#
# This file is the container analog of security/vulnerability-exceptions.
# toml: a reviewed, in-repo, justified suppression rather than a blind
# skip. Re-evaluate when the base image bumps its bundled build tooling
# (REL-002 digest pinning) — the entries should then disappear on their
# own.

# jaraco.context (vendored in setuptools): path traversal via malicious tar
CVE-2026-23949
# wheel: privilege escalation / arbitrary code execution via malicious wheel
CVE-2026-24049
